{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "SentinelOps",
          "semanticVersion": "1.0.0",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/mardromus/sentinelops",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "js.sqli.string-built-query",
              "name": "jsSqliStringBuiltQuery",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "SQL query built from strings"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The SQL text is concatenated with values, so input can change the query (SQL injection)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Pass values as parameters: db.query(\"SELECT ... WHERE id = ?\", [id]).\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\nCWE-89 SQL Injection: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html",
                "markdown": "Pass values as parameters: db.query(\"SELECT ... WHERE id = ?\", [id]).\n\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\n\nCWE-89 SQL Injection: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-89",
                  "owasp-a03:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "js.cmdi.shell-command-from-input",
              "name": "jsCmdiShellCommandFromInput",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Shell command built from variables"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A shell command string contains interpolated values; input can inject extra commands."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use execFile/spawn with an argument array and no shell.\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\nCWE-78 OS Command Injection: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html",
                "markdown": "Use execFile/spawn with an argument array and no shell.\n\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\n\nCWE-78 OS Command Injection: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-78",
                  "owasp-a03:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "js.code-injection.eval",
              "name": "jsCodeInjectionEval",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Dynamic code evaluation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Evaluating dynamic strings executes attacker-controlled code if any part comes from input."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Parse data with JSON.parse or a dedicated parser instead of evaluating it.\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\nCWE-95 Eval Injection: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/95.html",
                "markdown": "Parse data with JSON.parse or a dedicated parser instead of evaluating it.\n\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\n\nCWE-95 Eval Injection: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/95.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-95",
                  "owasp-a03:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "dep.CVE-2020-14343",
              "name": "depCVE202014343",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Vulnerable dependency (CVE-2020-14343)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "pyyaml 5.3.1 is affected by CVE-2020-14343 (Arbitrary code execution through full_load / FullLoader)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-14343",
              "help": {
                "text": "Upgrade pyyaml to 5.4 or later.\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\nA06:2021 Vulnerable and Outdated Components: https://owasp.org/Top10/A06_2021-Vulnerable_and_Outdated_Components/\nCWE-20 Improper Input Validation: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html",
                "markdown": "Upgrade pyyaml to 5.4 or later.\n\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\n\nA06:2021 Vulnerable and Outdated Components: https://owasp.org/Top10/A06_2021-Vulnerable_and_Outdated_Components/\n\nCWE-20 Improper Input Validation: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "dependency",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-20",
                  "owasp-a03:2021",
                  "owasp-a06:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "js.jwt.decode-without-verify",
              "name": "jsJwtDecodeWithoutVerify",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "JWT decoded without signature verification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "jwt.decode does not check the signature, so anyone can forge a token."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use jwt.verify(token, secret, { algorithms: [\"HS256\"] }).\nA07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/\nCWE-347 Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/347.html",
                "markdown": "Use jwt.verify(token, secret, { algorithms: [\"HS256\"] }).\n\nA07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/\n\nCWE-347 Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/347.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-347",
                  "owasp-a07:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "js.path-traversal.fs-from-input",
              "name": "jsPathTraversalFsFromInput",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "File path from request input"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A filesystem path is built from input, so \"../\" sequences can reach any file."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Resolve against a base directory and reject paths that escape it.\nA01:2021 Broken Access Control: https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/\nCWE-22 Path Traversal: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html",
                "markdown": "Resolve against a base directory and reject paths that escape it.\n\nA01:2021 Broken Access Control: https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/\n\nCWE-22 Path Traversal: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-22",
                  "owasp-a01:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "js.ssrf.fetch-from-input",
              "name": "jsSsrfFetchFromInput",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Server-side request to a user-supplied URL"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The server fetches whatever URL the client sends: internal services and cloud metadata become reachable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_%28SSRF%29/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Validate the URL, allow-list hosts and block private / link-local address ranges.\nA10:2021 Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF): https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_%28SSRF%29/\nCWE-918 Server-Side Request Forgery: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/918.html",
                "markdown": "Validate the URL, allow-list hosts and block private / link-local address ranges.\n\nA10:2021 Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF): https://owasp.org/Top10/A10_2021-Server-Side_Request_Forgery_%28SSRF%29/\n\nCWE-918 Server-Side Request Forgery: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/918.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-918",
                  "owasp-a10:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "js.xss.reflected-response",
              "name": "jsXssReflectedResponse",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Request input written into the HTML response"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "User input is reflected in the response without encoding (cross-site scripting)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/",
              "help": {
                "text": "HTML-encode the value or render it through a template engine that escapes by default.\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\nCWE-79 Cross-site Scripting: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html",
                "markdown": "HTML-encode the value or render it through a template engine that escapes by default.\n\nA03:2021 Injection: https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection/\n\nCWE-79 Cross-site Scripting: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-79",
                  "owasp-a03:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "js.prototype-pollution.merge-input",
              "name": "jsPrototypePollutionMergeInput",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Deep merge of request input"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Merging client objects deeply lets \"__proto__\" keys pollute every object in the process."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Copy only expected fields, or merge into Object.create(null) after rejecting __proto__/constructor.\nA08:2021 Software and Data Integrity Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures/\nCWE-1321 Prototype Pollution: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1321.html",
                "markdown": "Copy only expected fields, or merge into Object.create(null) after rejecting __proto__/constructor.\n\nA08:2021 Software and Data Integrity Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures/\n\nCWE-1321 Prototype Pollution: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1321.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-1321",
                  "owasp-a08:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "secret.connection-string",
              "name": "secretConnectionString",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Credentials in connection string"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Credentials in connection string committed in src/config.js. Anyone with read access to the repository or its history can use it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Revoke and rotate the credential now (it is in git history), then load it from the environment or a secret manager.\nA07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/\nCWE-798 Hard-coded Credentials: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html",
                "markdown": "Revoke and rotate the credential now (it is in git history), then load it from the environment or a secret manager.\n\nA07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/\n\nCWE-798 Hard-coded Credentials: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "secret",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-798",
                  "owasp-a07:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "py.deserialization.unsafe",
              "name": "pyDeserializationUnsafe",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unsafe deserialisation (pickle / yaml.load)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Deserialising untrusted data can execute code."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use json, or yaml.safe_load.\nA08:2021 Software and Data Integrity Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures/\nCWE-502 Deserialization of Untrusted Data: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html",
                "markdown": "Use json, or yaml.safe_load.\n\nA08:2021 Software and Data Integrity Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A08_2021-Software_and_Data_Integrity_Failures/\n\nCWE-502 Deserialization of Untrusted Data: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "sast",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-502",
                  "owasp-a08:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "secret.env-file-value",
              "name": "secretEnvFileValue",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hard-coded credential"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hard-coded credential committed in .env (assigned to DB_PASSWORD). Anyone with read access to the repository or its history can use it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Revoke and rotate the credential now (it is in git history), then load it from the environment or a secret manager.\nA07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/\nCWE-798 Hard-coded Credentials: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html",
                "markdown": "Revoke and rotate the credential now (it is in git history), then load it from the environment or a secret manager.\n\nA07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures: https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures/\n\nCWE-798 Hard-coded Credentials: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "secret",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-798",
                  "owasp-a07:2021"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
